# Live desktop verification (owner rule)

Unit/integration tests going green is **necessary but not sufficient**. For any
behavioural UI or MIDI/hardware-facing change, verify on the **real desktop app**
by exercising the **same controls a person uses**.

## Required

1. Build or run the native app (`XPPatchStudio.bat` option 2, or equivalent release build) when the change ships in the exe.
2. Drive the **actual window**: click pads, menus, tabs, knobs — not only invoke Tauri commands, call store methods, or poke WebView APIs as the sole proof.
3. Confirm the user-visible result (sound, LCD/pad lighting, status text, list contents). For Bank/MIDI paths, hear or observe the instrument when one is connected.
4. If the open app has no debugger port, restart with remote debugging only as an aid to click/observe — still click the real UI; do not treat IPC-only scripts as acceptance.

## Not enough alone

- Vitest / `cargo test` green
- Calling `followBankPad`, `selectSound`, or `invoke(...)` from a harness without opening the window
- “Should work” inferred from code review

## When reporting done

State what you clicked in the running app and what you observed. If live UI check was blocked (no rebuild, MIDI port held), say so explicitly — do not mark the behaviour verified.
